---
import Chapter from '../Chapter.astro';

const domains = [
  { d: 'A', posture: 'Classical', algs: 'RSA, ECDSA', tau: '1', cls: 'classical' },
  { d: 'B', posture: 'Hybrid', algs: 'Composite ECDSA + ML-DSA', tau: '0.3', cls: 'hybrid' },
  { d: 'C', posture: 'Post-quantum', algs: 'ML-DSA', tau: '0', cls: 'pq' },
];

const next = [
  ['Dominance as a theorem', 'proving the transition monotone against RFC 5280, §6.1.3 and §6.1.4.'],
  ['The common log, built', 'then several independent logs, signed post-quantum.'],
  ['Heterogeneity inside a domain', 'hierarchies whose root and intermediates use different algorithms.'],
  ['A post-quantum channel', 'from the PKI and the graph to the key exchange of the channel.'],
  ['Time, fully', 'when a datum is valid and when it becomes known, and how the graph evolves.'],
];
---

<Chapter id="laboratory" num="11" kicker="Laboratory" title="Three real PKI domains, one reproducible laboratory.">
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Three EJBCA Community Edition instances on Proxmox, each a PKI domain with its own
      cryptographic profile, cross-certified with one another. <strong>Certificates are issued for
      real, and every constraint of Φ is read from real extensions</strong>, never simulated.
    </p>
  </div>

  <table class="domains">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Domain</th>
        <th scope="col">Posture</th>
        <th scope="col">Algorithms</th>
        <th scope="col" class="num">Reference τ<sub>d</sub></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {
        domains.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <td>
              <span class={`dot dot--${r.cls}`} />
              {r.d}
            </td>
            <td>{r.posture}</td>
            <td>{r.algs}</td>
            <td class="num">{r.tau}</td>
          </tr>
        ))
      }
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="stack small">
    <span class="label">Stack</span>
    .NET on Kestrel · BouncyCastle .NET with native ML-DSA · PostgreSQL · Cytoscape.js · Ansible ·
    Linux containers, no proprietary licences
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="small muted">
      The evaluation measures and describes; it claims no performance improvement. The selected
      path is checked against exhaustive enumeration on small topologies and against a reference
      validation library, and a negative result counts as a result.
    </p>
  </div>


  <div class="next">
    <p class="label">Next lines of research</p>
    <ul>
      {
        next.map(([t, d]) => (
          <li>
            <strong>{t}:</strong> {d}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </div>
</Chapter>

<style>
  .domains {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .domains th,
  .domains td {
    padding: 0.7rem 1rem 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    text-align: left;
  }
  .domains th {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .domains td {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .domains .num {
    text-align: right;
    padding-right: 0;
  }
  .dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    margin-right: 0.6rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    vertical-align: 0.1em;
  }
  .dot--classical {
    background: var(--classical);
  }
  .dot--hybrid {
    background: var(--hybrid);
  }
  .dot--pq {
    background: var(--pq);
  }

  .stack {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .stack .label {
    margin-right: 0.8rem;
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .next {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .next ul {
    margin: 0.8rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }
  .next li {
    padding: 0.55rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .domains th:nth-child(3),
    .domains td:nth-child(3) {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
